  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A French Christian or a Muslim first name, a family name from the father, and often a traditional name too. Baoulé and Agni children get a day name for the day they were born (Kouassi or Akissi on Sunday, Kouadio or Adjoua on Monday, Konan or Amenan on Tuesday, Kouakou or Ahou on Wednesday, Yao or Aya on Thursday, Koffi or Affoué on Friday, Kouamé or Amoin on Saturday), and many family names are a father's day name. Dioula and Malinke families of the north are mostly Muslim, with names like Ouattara, Koné and Bamba. On forms and at school the family name comes first: 'Kouassi Yao Serge'.",
    "groups": {
      "akan": {
        "given": {
          "m": ["Kouassi", "Kouadio", "Konan", "Kouakou", "Yao", "Koffi", "Kouamé", "N'Guessan", "N'Dri", "Brou", "Kanga", "Kra", "Yoboué", "N'Goran"],
